2. openevidence-mcp — https://github.com/htlin222/openevidence-mcp
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The browser-relay transport concept used by `mcp/server.py` — running OpenEvidence
API calls inside the user's own already-logged-in browser tab rather than scraping
the site — originates with `openevidence-mcp` by Hsieh-Ting Lin (Apache-2.0).

No code from that project is reproduced here: it is TypeScript, this is Python, and
the transports are independently implemented. The idea, however, is his, and this
project follows from it.
